{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  PD TREATMENT — PLACEHOLDER (pipeline proof, NOT the real scoring algorithm)
  ============================================================================
  App embed block: injects assets/pd-treatment.js on every storefront page.
  The script asks /apps/pd/assign (the app proxy) which arm
  (control/treatment) the visitor is in for the collection they're viewing
  (using the SAME assignment logic as event tracking — see
  app/utils/experiments.server.ts) and, for treatment visitors only, reorders
  the collection grid by redirecting to the same URL with
  ?sort_by=created-descending (Shopify's native per-request sort override —
  it does NOT change the collection's saved default order).

  Everything here is deliberately trivial and easy to revert: delete this
  extension (or disable the "PD treatment (placeholder)" app embed in the
  theme editor) and every visitor sees the merchant's default order again.

  NOTE: the merchant must enable this block once via Theme editor →
  App embeds → "PD treatment (placeholder)". Until then the script is not
  loaded and all visitors see the default order.
{%- endcomment -%}

<script src="{{ 'pd-treatment.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PD treatment (placeholder)",
  "target": "body",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}